{
  "case_id": "2019-17-834",
  "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Schmidt",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In a typical and recent year, more than 15 million Americans became victims of identity theft."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Schmidt",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our laws apply in all settings to all people, citizen and alien alike."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But isn't it telling, General Schmidt, that in all three cases that we have, the prosecutor initially charged false Social Security number on the I-9, and it was only when the prosecutor appreciated that that couldn't be done that the I-9 charge was deleted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher G. Michel",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents stole the identity information of others and passed it off as their own on tax withholding forms. There's no dispute that states could traditionally prosecute frauds and forgeries of that kind."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Could you do this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0001-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the allegation in the criminal cases here, I think, were that the people, the defendants, were aliens and that, moreover, they submitted the information from the I-9 form -- it didn't say I-9 form, but it was from the I-9 form -- and they submitted it to get a job."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What type of --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, Mr. Hughes, it just seems a -- a -- a little bit odd to look to, you know, particular statements that Kansas made in order to determine whether a particular prosecution is preempted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hughes",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HUGHES: Your Honor, we argue both express preemption on the language of 1324a(b)(5) as well as conflict with -- or, sorry, with -- as well as implied, with respect to implied --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How is it expressly preempted under (b)(5)? That argument mystifies me, because (b)(5) says nothing about work authorization. It says nothing about aliens. It says nothing about the use of the information by a state government or by the federal government. It applies to any use."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Schmidt",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f231afc29465b041de3f8296f5c21018ca192664b1786802c3f41ac7e05a712f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f231afc29465-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "With respect to Justice Alito's line of questioning on the (b)(5) language, (b)(5) is certainly, if read as a preemption provision, most unusual, at -- not least of which is because it is not aimed exclusively at states."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-17-834",
